> gf2matrix (x & 0x0f) ^ ((x & 0x30) >> 2) u8
  note: ^ is xor here (addition in GF(2))
the GF(2) matrix of (x & 0x0f) ^ ((x & 0x30) >> 2) on u8 (row i = output bit i, column j = input bit j, bit 0 first)
  [1.......]
  [.1......]
  [..1.1...]
  [...1.1..]
  [........]
  [........]
  [........]
  [........]
  how: the columns are f(1 << j); check: f(x) = M x for every x (256 inputs)
  rank 4: singular (some values collide; the kernel has dimension w - rank)
  characteristic polynomial: x^8 + x^4 = (x)^4 (x + 1)^4
